    commonQuestions: faq("Ace of Wands", { yes: "The Ace of Wands often leans yes when the situation benefits from initiative, courage, and a fresh beginning. It is not a guarantee of lasting success; the spark needs practical follow-through, enough energy, and a willingness to learn as the idea takes shape.", positive: "The Ace of Wands is generally energizing because it restores possibility and creative momentum. Its challenge is to distinguish meaningful inspiration from the urge to escape boredom through another beginning. Its potential becomes positive through commitment, not excitement alone.", person: "As a person, the Ace of Wands can describe someone inventive, enthusiastic, bold, and eager to begin. In shadow, they may be impulsive, easily distracted, or more attached to the rush of possibility than to the steady work a relationship or project requires.", advice: "Act while the energy is available, but choose a step small enough to complete. Give the idea a container: time on the calendar, a first conversation, a prototype, or a concrete learning goal. Discipline does not kill the spark; it gives it a future.", reversed: "Reversed, the Ace of Wands warns of depleted enthusiasm, blocked creativity, poor timing, or a pattern of abandoning beginnings. Look for the missing condition rather than forcing inspiration. It may be time to rest, clarify your purpose, or reduce competing commitments.", repeated: "A repeating Ace of Wands may show that a creative impulse keeps asking for a response. It can also reveal a cycle of collecting exciting beginnings. Notice whether you are being invited to start something new or to finally nourish the spark already in your hands." }),
    variants: variant("Ace of Wands", "ace-of-wands", "01", { subtitle: "A spark becomes a path when you choose to feed it.", astralVeilMeaning: "The Ace of Wands appears before form, certainty, or proof. It is the moment energy recognizes a direction it might become. Inspiration opens the threshold, but only continued attention can transform that opening into a living creation.", reflectionPrompts: ["What idea continues returning because it wants to be explored?", "What small action would give this inspiration somewhere to grow?"] }, { subtitle: "Not every flame is a calling; some only reveal what you are trying to escape.", astralVeilMeaning: "The Ace of Wands enters Veilfall where excitement is mistaken for direction. A new beginning can feel powerful because it temporarily frees the self from boredom, doubt, or unfinished responsibility. The flame must be examined before it is allowed to consume the path.", reflectionPrompts: ["Which new beginning am I pursuing mainly for the feeling of escape?", "What unfinished commitment loses my attention whenever something more exciting appears?"] })
