    categories: { love: { upright: "Shared joy, a milestone, or a feeling of home can strengthen a connection. Single people may be drawn toward communities where relationship feels more possible; partners may benefit from recognizing what they have built. Celebration becomes intimate when it includes everyone’s real experience, not only a pleasing image.", reversed: "Family tension, unsupported plans, or uncertainty about belonging may be affecting the relationship. Do not demand harmony at the cost of honesty. A delayed celebration can still be meaningful if the underlying strain, exclusion, or practical instability is given patient attention." }, career: { upright: "A project may reach a milestone worth recognizing with the people who helped create it. The Four supports team cohesion, a stable work environment, and rituals that mark progress. Celebrate success while documenting what made it possible so the foundation can support the next stage.", reversed: "Workplace tension or weak infrastructure may be hidden beneath a successful appearance. Review roles, resources, and communication before assuming a win is secure. Private achievement can still matter, but the card invites attention to whether the environment is genuinely supportive and sustainable." }, feelings: { upright: "Feelings may be warm, settled, and open to shared enjoyment. Someone could be ready to welcome you into their everyday life or to mark a meaningful step together. Look for inclusion, consistency, and ease rather than treating celebration alone as proof of long-term security.", reversed: "A person may feel excluded, unsettled, or unable to relax into a connection that looks stable from the outside. Their hesitation may reflect real tension or differing expectations about belonging. A direct, gentle conversation can reveal what support is missing." }, advice: { upright: "Pause long enough to acknowledge what has been built. Share gratitude, create a small ritual, and strengthen the relationships or systems that supported the progress. The Four of Wands favors joy that is rooted in care, not a rush to move past the milestone.", reversed: "Attend to the foundation before staging the celebration. Name any tension, repair practical gaps, and make room for voices that have been overlooked. Belonging becomes more trustworthy when it does not require anyone to hide discomfort in order to preserve a harmonious appearance." }, spiritual: { upright: "The Four of Wands supports gratitude practiced in community and in place. Notice the people, routines, and spaces that help you feel held. Spiritual belonging is not conformity; it is the experience of being able to participate without abandoning your particular self.", reversed: "A spiritual group or ideal of home may be asking for honest examination. Do not confuse a beautiful ritual with a healthy foundation. Seek environments where questions, differences, and repair are possible alongside celebration and shared meaning." }, },
    journey: { currentCard: "Four of Wands", details: [{ label: "Stage", value: "The Sanctuary" }, { label: "Gift", value: "Belonging" }, { label: "Lesson", value: "Honor progress and strengthen its foundation" }, { label: "Risk", value: "False harmony" }], nextCard: "Five of Wands", nextMessage: "Stability is tested by friction, competition, and difference.", summary: "The Three of Wands expands intention into the wider world. The Four of Wands pauses to create belonging and celebrate progress, while the Five of Wands introduces the friction that appears when multiple desires, identities, and ambitions occupy the same space." },
    commonQuestions: faq("Four of Wands", { yes: "The Four of Wands often leans yes for gatherings, milestones, shared plans, and efforts to establish stability. Its encouragement is strongest when the foundation is real. Celebrate, but also check whether the practical and relational conditions can support what is being welcomed.", positive: "The Four of Wands is generally affirming because it recognizes belonging, support, and a moment of earned joy. It is not a command to perform happiness. Its deeper lesson is that celebration is most nourishing when it includes honesty, inclusion, and continued care.", person: "As a person, the Four of Wands can describe someone welcoming, community-minded, celebratory, and skilled at creating a sense of home. In shadow, they may prioritize appearances, avoid conflict, or define belonging so narrowly that difference is quietly excluded.", advice: "Recognize the milestone and invest in the foundation beneath it. Let people know they matter, mark the progress, and address the practical detail that will make the next stage more stable. Joy grows when it is rooted rather than merely displayed.", reversed: "Reversed, the Four of Wands warns of family tension, uncertain belonging, postponed celebration, or a foundation that needs attention. Do not paper over discomfort. Clarify expectations and make repairs before relying on an image of harmony to carry the situation.", repeated: "A repeating Four of Wands can ask where you are ready to receive support and celebrate progress. It may also reveal a recurring tension between authentic belonging and the pressure to fit a community, family, or relationship image that does not fully include you." }),
